      "text": [
        " : سَأَلْتُ أَبَا إِبْرَاهِيمَ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ عَنِ اَلْمَرْوَةِ وَ اَلْقَصَبَةِ وَ اَلْعُودِ يَذْبَحُ بِهِنَّ اَلْإِنْسَانُ إِذَا لَمْ يَجِدْ سِكِّيناً فَقَالَ \"إِذَا فَرَى اَلْأَوْدَاجَ فَلاَ بَأْسَ بِذَلِكَ \"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.4163 - Safwan ibn Yahya narrated from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hajjaj who said: I asked Abu Ibrahim (Imam Musa ibn Jafar Al-Kadhim (as)) about using a flint, a reed, or a piece of wood to slaughter an animal if one does not have a knife.\nImam (as) said: \"If it cuts the veins, then there is no harm in it.\""
        ]
      }
